// A positional constructor pattern lists one name for each field of the
// constructor; more names is a compile error (spec/02-syntax.md, Extended
// match arm patterns). Probe 139 checks fewer names.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The try makes a
// run-time fault print, so an implementation that runs the program fails
// this probe.
enum E { A(x, y) }
try {
    print match E.A(1, 2) { case E.A(p, q, r) => p case _ => 0 };
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
